# Story 21: Cross-Pane Coordination (50s)
# Hook: Name your panes, then let AI inspect and coordinate across them.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-21-cross-pane.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- you land in shell mode.

[00:04.0 --> 00:08.0]
Open a second pane. Ctrl+P enters pane mode, then n splits right.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
We are in the left pane. Name it 'builder' with the ##pane name command.

[00:13.0 --> 00:18.0]
Tab moves to the next pane. Name this one 'tester'.

[00:18.0 --> 00:23.0]
Back in the builder pane. Run a build command.

[00:23.0 --> 00:28.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode.

[00:28.0 --> 00:40.0]
Ask the AI to look at another pane by name. It can read the content of any named pane.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
The AI reads the tester pane's content and reports back. Cross-pane coordination -- your AI sees the full workspace.

[00:45.0 --> 00:50.0]
Named panes + AI inspection = coordinated workflows.

